pokebw2-allocsizes.patch (tools/pokebw2_fetch.sh, the maintainers' notes): three allocations give the DS size of what holds
pointers, so on a 64-bit host the block is too small: the field's prop search (FieldPropSystem_FindPropsInArea's 32
pointers, 0x80 bytes on the DS; Black's src/ov021/field_buildmodel.c has 32 * sizeof(FieldChunkPropHolder *)), the
C-Gear help's CGHelpParam (8 on the DS, 0x10 here) and the Battle Subway script's BSubwayScrWork (0x7f0, 0x840 here).
Each is the sizeof of what it holds. From a scan of the allocations with a number for their size against the host's
sizeof of the pointer's type (the maintainers' notes).

diff --git a/src/ov033/bsubway_scr.c b/src/ov033/bsubway_scr.c
index a6b2604..8305be6 100644
--- a/src/ov033/bsubway_scr.c
+++ b/src/ov033/bsubway_scr.c
@@ -56,7 +56,7 @@ BSubwayScrWork *BsubwayScr_CreateWork(GameSystem *gsys, u16 resume, u16 playMode
     gameData = GSYS_GetGameData(gsys);
     playerInfo = GetGameDataPlayerInfo(gameData);
     save = GameData_GetSaveControl(gameData);
-    bsw = GFL_HeapAllocate(4, 0x7f0, 1, "bsubway_scr.c", 0x5f);
+    bsw = GFL_HeapAllocate(4, sizeof(BSubwayScrWork), 1, "bsubway_scr.c", 0x5f);
     bsw->heapId = 4;
     bsw->magic = 0x12345678;
     bsw->gameData = gameData;
